WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.559
Okay, you've reached the end of the course, and I want to close this out properly.

2
00:00:05.119 --> 00:00:09.520
You've worked through every domain on the exam blueprint, taken practice exams,

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.840
and reviewed your results. That's the work most candidates skip, and it's exactly why

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.639
you're going to be in a stronger position on exam day than the average developer walking in cold.

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.200
Before we officially wrap up, I've got a few more things I want you to hear

6
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.680
that'll set you up for the exam itself and for everything that comes after this credential.

7
00:00:28.399 --> 00:00:34.240
First, don't stop practicing. Practice exams are the single highest return activity you can do

8
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.119
between now and your exam date. Every additional practice exam strengthens your architectural

9
00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:44.799
judgment, improves your timing, and exposes you to more scenario types. The more scenarios you've

10
00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:49.919
seen, the fewer surprises you'll encounter on the real exam. If you haven't already,

11
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:55.119
pick up the six-exam practice course. Fresh questions, progressive difficulty calibrated

12
00:00:55.119 --> 00:00:59.840
against the official blueprint. There's no point of diminishing returns here. The more reps you put

13
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:05.839
in, the better your odds. And because CCAF has a six-month recertification cycle, you'll be coming

14
00:01:05.839 --> 00:01:11.360
back for refresher practice every renewal window. The practice library scales and changes with the

15
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:17.680
exam blueprint and follows you on your journey of recertification. One last thing before you go.

16
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:23.680
Thank you for sticking with this course. CCAF is a real commitment, and the fact that you made it

17
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.639
all the way through tells me something about how serious you are about this certification and the

18
00:01:28.639 --> 00:01:33.599
industry. That commitment is what separates the developers who pass from the ones who don't.

19
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.480
Make sure you collect your course completion certificate. If you're earning CPE credits

20
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:44.559
for any related certification, this might qualify for that, so save it either way. And when you pass

21
00:01:44.559 --> 00:01:50.400
that exam, I would genuinely love to hear about it. Connect with me on LinkedIn, tag me in a post.

22
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.319
I celebrate every one of those wins, and the CCAF cohort grows stronger with every named pass.

23
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.680
Remember, your enrollment covers every recertification cycle. The content updates

24
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:08.080
continuously. The question bank grows every month. And I'll see you back here in six months. All right,

25
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.880
you've done the work. Trust your preparation, and go build something great with what you've learned.

26
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.839
I'll see you later.

